The rust png codec cannot be built for Android out of the box. Two lists in
MODULE.bazel leave out aarch64-linux-android:

- rust.toolchain extra_target_triples: no Rust standard library for the target.
- crate.from_specs supported_platform_triples: crate_universe marks every crate
  (cxx first) incompatible with //bazel/platform:android_arm64, and analysis
  stops with "Target //rust/png:ffi_rs is incompatible".

cargo_bindeps is left alone. cxxbridge-cmd runs on the exec platform (linux
x86_64), not on the target.

Checked on Skia 152 (0873ec164a) under WSL2 Ubuntu 24.04:
  bazelisk build //rust/png:ffi_rs --platforms=//bazel/platform:android_arm64
gives libffi_rs.a whose 960 objects are all ELF64 AArch64.

